1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,040
Finally we are ready to set up our dbt project Let's do this

2
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:10,209
Ensure that your virtual lamp is activated

3
00:00:10,209 --> 00:00:12,513
and we will go and say dbt init

4
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:21,465
and one important piece I'm gonna get back to this in a second is skip profile setup

5
00:00:21,465 --> 00:00:24,045
and then our project name

6
00:00:24,045 --> 00:00:29,225
and our project name is rbnb Please execute this

7
00:00:29,225 --> 00:00:34,480
one of course you will find this command in the course resources markdown

8
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:39,160
Okay it's up and running

9
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:44,453
Let's open this folder in your editor

10
00:00:44,453 --> 00:00:50,275
which in my case is Visual Studio Code

11
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:53,504
You can see that we have a bunch of subfolders and files in this folder

12
00:00:53,504 --> 00:00:58,400
which of course we will explore in great detail later in the course

13
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:05,793
For now let's just take the profiles yaml that you downloaded from the dbt setup app

14
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,797
and copy it into this folder

15
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:12,115
I will go and simply drag and drop it in there

16
00:01:12,115 --> 00:01:17,600
but you can just copy and paste it in there in any way you like

17
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:21,424
The main thing is that you want to end up with a profiles yaml

18
00:01:21,424 --> 00:01:25,599
which has all the connection details to Snowflake

19
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,436
Let's see if it works

20
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:30,252
First of all as you open the editor

21
00:01:30,252 --> 00:01:34,191
you might want to re enable your virtual environment

22
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:37,274
As you can see mine has been already re enabled

23
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:43,718
And now you can say dbt debug So execute dbt debug

24
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:47,515
dbt debug will take a look at your project

25
00:01:47,515 --> 00:01:54,467
and tell you if the whole file structure and everything is consistent

26
00:01:54,467 --> 00:01:59,279
and if it can connect to your data warehouse

27
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:03,076
It should only take a second or two to execute

28
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:06,201
And it says that our profiles file is okay

29
00:02:06,201 --> 00:02:10,000
our dbt project yaml is okay Git is found

30
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,541
If you don't have Git installed you might see an error

31
00:02:13,541 --> 00:02:14,868
or Git not found here

32
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,518
Don't worry about that for now

33
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,915
You don't need Git for the core part of this course

34
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:22,636
Then it tells you all about the connections

35
00:02:22,636 --> 00:02:25,126
and it tries to connect to Snowflake

36
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:29,078
If you see connection okay you're golden

37
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:33,419
If you have problems connecting to Snowflake when you execute dbt debug

38
00:02:33,419 --> 00:02:37,823
the most common issues are that you are either behind the VPN

39
00:02:37,823 --> 00:02:43,399
or that you are behind a corporate proxy or a corporate firewall

40
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:47,002
In this case I would like to ask you to switch off the VPN

41
00:02:47,002 --> 00:02:50,369
and ensure that you use a laptop and a network

42
00:02:50,369 --> 00:02:54,691
that provides you with unconstrained network access

43
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:57,691
So you might want to use your personal laptop

44
00:02:57,691 --> 00:03:00,432
in your run into issues or just switch wifi

45
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:07,155
and use a wifi network that doesn't constrain your network access

46
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:11,354
Let's talk a bit about why we use the skip profile setup switch

47
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:16,008
We did this because by default dbt tries to setup

48
00:03:16,008 --> 00:03:19,750
your profile file not in your project folder

49
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:22,000
but in your home folder

50
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,058
For earlier dbt versions the default location

51
00:03:25,058 --> 00:03:32,719
for your profiles folder was a folder called dbt inside your home folder

52
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:35,020
This has changed with recent dbt versions

53
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:38,960
and now your default profiles folder is your project folder

54
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:41,196
But I want to discuss a little bit about it

55
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:45,480
So by default you would go to your home folder

56
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:49,101
dbt folder both in windows and on a mac

57
00:03:49,101 --> 00:03:51,720
and here you would find a profile siamak

58
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:55,108
Now you won't find it here and that's ok

59
00:03:55,108 --> 00:03:57,880
I just set this up for you for demo

60
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:02,099
And the reason behind this was that generally speaking

61
00:04:02,099 --> 00:04:05,656
you don't want to pack your connection details

62
00:04:05,656 --> 00:04:09,946
which has your private key and other sensitive information

63
00:04:09,946 --> 00:04:14,200
in your project folder because you don't want to submit it to git

64
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:17,280
and of course your connection might be different

65
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:20,197
depending on if you are on your own laptop

66
00:04:20,197 --> 00:04:22,871
or if you are on a production server

67
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,800
So if you work with production dbt apps

68
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:30,180
I would suggest you to either copy the profile siamak

69
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:34,821
to your project folder automatically through a CICD pipeline

70
00:04:34,821 --> 00:04:38,578
and exclude it from git so never submit it

71
00:04:38,578 --> 00:04:42,189
or just use it in an arbitrary location

72
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,816
Regardless where you have your profile siamak

73
00:04:44,816 --> 00:04:48,881
you can always execute dbt with the dash profile dr parameter

74
00:04:48,881 --> 00:04:52,955
which specifies the path to your profile siamak

75
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:57,368
In this course for simplicity we use the profile siamak's default location

76
00:04:57,368 --> 00:05:00,080
which is our project folder

77
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:03,018
So let's take a look at the profile siamak file

78
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:05,533
The profile siamak has a profile name

79
00:05:05,533 --> 00:05:09,052
which we will reference later in our project file

80
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:11,618
so we know which profile to use

81
00:05:11,618 --> 00:05:14,176
and then dbt can have multiple targets

82
00:05:14,176 --> 00:05:16,676
for example you can have a target

83
00:05:16,676 --> 00:05:19,661
so a connection to your dev environment

84
00:05:19,661 --> 00:05:21,830
and we would have like a QA

85
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:26,394
for testing and a prode environment if you wish

86
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:30,390
Here in this example we only have a dev environment for now

87
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:34,182
so we have a single target which is called dev

88
00:05:34,182 --> 00:05:37,916
and also we are setting this as a default target

89
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:42,075
And everything that comes in between is your connection detail

90
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:44,462
We use a snowflake type connection

91
00:05:44,462 --> 00:05:46,367
this is our snowflake account

92
00:05:46,367 --> 00:05:50,008
we are authenticating with the dbt user that we set up

93
00:05:50,008 --> 00:05:52,217
which has the role transform

94
00:05:52,217 --> 00:05:56,797
it's again a role that we set up with the automatic setup script

95
00:05:56,800 --> 00:06:00,136
Here is a private key that the setup script generated for us

96
00:06:00,136 --> 00:06:03,400
and the private key also has a passphrase

97
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,913
It is optional to have a passphrase

98
00:06:05,913 --> 00:06:08,676
but our BI tool will require a private key

99
00:06:08,676 --> 00:06:11,304
which is protected by a passphrase

100
00:06:11,304 --> 00:06:15,032
so I just added a single digit Q as a passphrase

101
00:06:15,032 --> 00:06:18,000
when we generated our private key

102
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,450
The database we want to use is Airbnb

103
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:23,635
this is because our automated snowflake setup

104
00:06:23,635 --> 00:06:26,394
set up an Airbnb database for us

105
00:06:26,394 --> 00:06:28,594
with a schema called row

106
00:06:28,594 --> 00:06:34,480
which has all the host listing and reviews tables

107
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,622
And the output schemas will be dev

108
00:06:36,622 --> 00:06:42,100
so this is where we want to then later generate our tables

109
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:46,134
For the sake of simplicity we also instruct dbt

110
00:06:46,134 --> 00:06:49,495
to only work on one model at a time

111
00:06:49,495 --> 00:06:53,897
so we don't get into parallel execution problems

112
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:58,350
And in snowflake there is a default data warehouse that we will use

113
00:06:58,350 --> 00:07:01,000
and it is called compute wh

114
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,540
This is how our profile server has been set up

115
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:07,490
and now you are up and running with dbt

116
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:12,155
There is one last but very important thing to avoid any confusion

117
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,468
I'm going to use sometimes VisioStudio cost terminal

118
00:07:15,468 --> 00:07:20,157
and sometimes standalone terminal application It doesn't matter right

119
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:23,525
I would suggest you just use VisioStudio cost terminal

120
00:07:23,525 --> 00:07:27,117
because that gives you even if you are on windows

121
00:07:27,117 --> 00:07:32,432
the closest experience to my environment here on a Mac

122
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:35,932
And another super important detail is that

123
00:07:35,932 --> 00:07:41,160
you will see sometimes Airbnb here as my project folder name

124
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:45,960
but sometimes you will see dbt learn

125
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:52,424
The reason for that is that recently dbt labs has trademarked the dbt learn term

126
00:07:52,424 --> 00:07:57,112
so now in the new videos I go with the Airbnb project name

127
00:07:57,112 --> 00:08:03,115
but in some earlier videos you will see that the folder I work on is dbt learn

128
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:07,188
It doesn't matter you will always see Airbnb

129
00:08:07,188 --> 00:08:10,239
and everything will work 100 the same

130
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,875
So let's move on and get our hands dirty with dbt
